# Helpers that name an operator in a refusal, and the name each one uses.
#
# A helper shared by several operators cannot name one of them in its
# refusal without reporting that name to all the others: PLRM 3.11.1 has
# $error /command hold what was executing, and a program reads it to learn
# which operator it called went wrong. Three helpers were doing exactly
# that and now take the caller's name instead (.instof, .imagepaintm and
# .customcolorspace); tests/operator_identity_test.ps holds them to it by
# provoking each refusal from each operator.
#
# What remains here is the population that still names an operator
# outright, so that a new one -- or a changed name -- is looked at rather
# than landing unread. A row is fine when every route to the helper really
# is that operator, and most of these are: the halftone helpers are reached
# only under sethalftone, the shading ones only under shfill, the CID ones
# only under show. Two rows are fine for a different reason: .endpage names
# the page-device procedure that returned the wrong type, not its caller,
# and .upathcheck names uappend because ufill, ueofill and ustroke call the
# uappend operator itself.
#
# One row is a known defect, left as it is on purpose. crossdashbound names
# stroke, and strokepath reaches the dash-count limit without stroke
# running -- but stroke also calls strokepath internally when the device
# will not take a path, so threading the name makes the reported operator
# depend on the output device. Fixing it means threading the top-level
# operator through stroke's own use of strokepath.
#
# helper                    names
.checkpagefeatures          setpagedevice
.checkpagehandlers          setpagedevice
.cidface                    show
.csvalidate                 setcolorspace
.endpage                    EndPage
.fmapnext                   show
.fneval                     shfill
.fneval2                    shfill
.fnsampled                  shfill
.htcelllimit                sethalftone
.htextent                   sethalftone
.htoptional                 sethalftone
.htrequire                  sethalftone
.htvalidate                 sethalftone
.meshsh                     shfill
.mrdflag                    shfill
.mrdinit                    shfill
.spacereduce                setcolorspace
.upathcheck                 uappend
.withspacebody              setcolor
crossdashbound              stroke
doclip                      clip
loadgraphics                setpagedevice
